Key findings summary:

- **1 critical**: Missing CSV entries for "Air Conditioner" and "GSHP" equipment types — multi-speed standalone ACs and ground-source heat pumps silently fail to get per-stage capacity/COP data
- **2 high**: All MSHP Cooler/Heater rows have no capacity ratio of 1.0 (all max at 1.2, violating EnergyPlus rated-speed convention); MSHP SHR/capacity ratios identically replicated across 20 SEER tiers suggesting copied rather than measured data
- **4 medium**: Non-monotonic COP in 22/24 SEER ASHP Cooler, anomalous COP in 14.5 SEER MSHP Cooler, 11.0 HSPF ASHP Heater COPs appear miscopied from ~9 HSPF unit, airflow ratios follow linear rather than cube-law fan power
- **2 low**: Sparse gas furnace tier coverage (only 80/90 AFUE), SHR source-inconsistency across "Manual" vs "testing_500" entries
